 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the analysis of wine composition, particularly focusing on the extraction of amino acids and volatile compounds. Sparkling Wines are composed of wine, and the extraction procedure involves the use of methanol and chloroform. The Agilent 7890A GC is used as an internal standard, and IMAC uses acetonitrile and formic acid. The analysis also involves the use of Waters vials and the determination of alcohol content. The volatile compounds influence the amino acids, and the wine accumulates ASN and depletes ORN.",
